# 11. How to use these prompts in Google AI Studio

Use the prompts in this order:

| Order | Prompt                  | Expected output                           |
| ----- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| 1     | Project audit           | Full understanding of existing repository |
| 2     | Intelligence engine     | Correct underlying analysis               |
| 3     | Product UI/UX           | Complete interactive interface            |
| 4     | Gemini integration      | Evidence interpretation                   |
| 5     | Backend and persistence | Working APIs and durable storage          |
| 6     | Functional verification | Test evidence and defect fixes            |
| 7     | Deployment              | Verified live application                 |

**Important working rules:**

* Keep the existing GitHub repository as the source of truth.
* Make changes in a separate branch.
* Commit after each successfully tested phase.
* Never overwrite the existing engine without reviewing it.
* Ask AI Studio to show the files it changed.
* Run tests after every major implementation stage.
* Do not accept screenshots as proof of functionality.
* Do not accept fabricated metrics or simulated experiment outcomes as real results.

### My strongest recommendation

Don't ask AI Studio to build all seven stages in one enormous generation. Use the seven prompts sequentially. After each stage, make it show the changed files, tests executed and outstanding defects before continuing.

**The final goal isn't a better-looking screenshot. It's a developer who can give TERRARIUM a real code change, run a real experiment, inspect the evidence, discover a genuine blind spot and understand exactly how much confidence to place in the result.**
